@startuml delivery-pipeline
!include ../diagram-style.puml
' docs/process/delivery-pipeline.html: from refinement to merge.
' Laid out by Graphviz (`dot`): the flow has two loops back to the developer.

rectangle "Suhay + Musti · joint grilling\nrefinement block: REQ, one Given-When-Then,\nADR check, scope, honesty check, risk tier" as A
rectangle "Stakeholder rules on the block" as A2
rectangle "Musti · Lead\nbreak down, dispatch" as B
rectangle "Kaan / Robin · Dev\nimplement tests-first, own gate green" as C
rectangle "Dev opens a DRAFT PR\nCI starts running here" as D
rectangle "Musti · Lead\nreviews on the draft, comments in public as Musti\nposts his record even when he finds nothing" as E
rectangle "Salih · QA\ntests per risk tier: T3 not at all,\nT2 if user-visible, T1 in full" as F
rectangle "Salih posts his test record\nand flips the PR to READY" as G
rectangle "Stakeholder · final human pass on GitHub → merge" as H

A --> A2
A2 --> B
B --> C
C --> D
D --> E : the draft itself is the trigger
E --> C : unresolved findings
E --> F : no unresolved findings
F --> C : fails
F --> G : passes
G --> H
@enduml
